# Issue before fix

For **every** user-submitted issue containing a bug or feature request:

1. **First**, create a GitHub issue using `gh issue create` (brief title + body: problem / expected behaviour / context / project).
2. **Project #9** (`korzhanov`, https://github.com/users/korzhanov/projects/9) — сразу после create:
   ```bash
   ITEM=$(gh project item-add 9 --owner korzhanov --url "$URL" --format json --jq .id)
   # Status: 🌀 MVP Backlog | ▶️ Todo | 👾 Realization | 👀 In review | ✅ Done
   gh project item-edit --id "$ITEM" --project-id PVT_kwHOACIdh84AEKzA \
     --field-id PVTSSF_lAHOACIdh84AEKzAzgCZrYw \
     --single-select-option-id e83e7f55   # MVP Backlog; Todo=47fc9ee4 Realization=68a253c3 Done=98236657
   ```
   Нужны scopes: `project` + `read:project` (`gh auth refresh -s read:project,project`).
3. Take ownership (comment/assign) if needed.
4. Only then implement the fix or feature.
5. Upon completion: summary comment + `gh issue close`; Status → **✅ Done** (`98236657`).

Progress / screenshots: **`issue-pr-progress-visual.mdc`**. PR checklist tree: **`pr-task-tree.mdc`**.

Do not skip the issue step ‘just to fix it faster’. Exception: purely informational queries that do not involve code changes.
